## Why This Is Asked
Tests for feature flags are essential to validate UI gating, state persistence, and how flows handle mid-flight flag changes in real user journeys.

## Key Concepts
- Feature flags and gating
- Test data seeding and API-driven state setup
- End-to-end verification of UI state and backend persistence
- Handling mid-flow toggling and UI consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('onboarding with feature flag', async ({ page, request }) => {
  // Seed user with onboarding flag ON
  await request.post('/api/test/setup-user', { data: { flagName: 'new-onboarding', value: true } });
  // Login and navigate
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.fill('#email', 'user@example.com');
  await page.fill('#password', 's3cret');
  await page.click('button[type="submit"]');
  await page.waitForURL('/dashboard');

  // Verify onboarding visible
  await expect(page.locator('#onboarding-panel')).toBeVisible();
  await expect(page.locator('#onboarding-panel .step')).toHaveCount(4);

  // Complete first step
  await page.click('#step-1 .complete');
  await expect(page.locator('#step-1')).toHaveClass(/completed/);

  // Refresh and verify persistence
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('#step-1')).toHaveClass(/completed/);

  // Turn flag OFF mid-flow and verify UI hides, but backend progress remains
  await request.post('/api/test/setup-user', { data: { flagName: 'new-onboarding', value: false } });
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('#onboarding-panel')).toBeHidden();

  // Validate backend progress still retrievable
  const res = await request.get('/api/user/progress');
  expect(res.status()).toBe(200);
  const data = await res.json();
  expect(data.stepsCompleted).toBe(1);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this test to run reliably in CI with parallelization?
- What considerations would you add for multiple feature flags interacting in the same flow?

## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to design a realistic E2E testing scenario involving per-user feature flags, UI state validation, and data persistence. It covers test data seeding with proper user isolation, mocking external dependencies, and validating analytics signals.

## Key Concepts
- Feature flag semantics for per-user progressive rollout
- Test data seeding with user isolation
- Mocking external services
- UI assertions and persistence across reloads
- Analytics event validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright E2E test
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test.describe('Notifications Center feature flag', () => {
  const enabledUser = { id: 'user-1', email: 'enabled@example.com', flags: { notificationsCenter: true } };
  const disabledUser = { id: 'user-2', email: 'disabled@example.com', flags: { notificationsCenter: false } };

  test('enabled user sees Notifications Center and receives sample notification', async ({ page }) => {
    await seedUser(enabledUser);
    await page.goto('/login');
    await page.fill('[name=email]', enabledUser.email);
    await page.fill('[name=password]', 'password123');
    await page.click('[type=submit]');

    await expect(page.locator('#notifications-panel')).toBeVisible();
    await expect(page.locator('.notification-item').first()).toContainText('Welcome to Notifications Center');
  });

  test('disabled user does not see Notifications Center', async ({ page }) => {
    await seedUser(disabledUser);
    await page.goto('/login');
    await page.fill('[name=email]', disabledUser.email);
    await page.fill('[name=password]', 'password123');
    await page.click('[type=submit]');

    await expect(page.locator('#notifications-panel')).not.toBeVisible();
  });

  test('flag toggle persists across reload', async ({ page }) => {
    await seedUser(enabledUser);
    await page.goto('/dashboard');
    await expect(page.locator('#notifications-panel')).toBeVisible();

    await mockFlagService.setFlag(enabledUser.id, 'notificationsCenter', false);
    await page.reload();

    await expect(page.locator('#notifications-panel')).not.toBeVisible();
  });

  test('analytics events emitted correctly', async ({ page }) => {
    const analyticsEvents = [];
    page.on('request', (req) => {
      if (req.url().includes('/analytics')) analyticsEvents.push(req.postData());
    });

    await seedUser(enabledUser);
    await page.goto('/dashboard');

    expect(analyticsEvents).toContainEqual(expect.objectContaining({ event: 'notifications_panel_opened' }));
  });
});
```

